# Definition of Done

A task or PR is **done** only when every box is checked. "It compiles" and
"it looks right" are not done. Evidence beats assertion — paste real output.

## Per task (one task from tasks.md)

- [ ] The active spec was read; the change stays within its approved boundary.
- [ ] **Under `tdd`/`tdd-e2e`:** a test failed (RED) for the expected reason before the
      implementation, when the task adds behavior; that test now passes (GREEN) and
      refactoring kept it green.
- [ ] **Under `unit`:** the behavior is covered by a unit test that passes (no RED-first
      evidence required).
- [ ] **Under `tdd-e2e`:** the end-to-end coverage for the affected golden/error flow runs green.
- [ ] The relevant suite, lint, and typecheck pass for the touched scope.
- [ ] Unit tests were run **through the csdd CLI** so the spec carries the evidence (**every flow**):
      `npx @protonspy/csdd spec test-report <feature> --run --lang <lang>` wrote `specs/<feature>/test-report.json`
      (tests green, coverage recorded, no open attentions). Missing this evidence is a blocked item.
- [ ] Scope was respected — no opportunistic refactors or unrelated changes.
- [ ] `## Implementation Notes` in tasks.md updated with any cross-task learning.
- [ ] Report lists: task ID, files changed, tests added, commands run, remaining risks.

## Per PR (a reviewable slice)

- [ ] Tests cover success, validation, authorization, and external-failure paths for new behavior.
- [ ] Full verification gate is green: tests, lint, typecheck, build.
- [ ] `code-reviewer` sub-agent ran and reported no open Blockers.
- [ ] For security-sensitive changes, `security-reviewer` ran and reported no Critical/High.
- [ ] The PR body carries evidence: spec links, tasks completed, the real verification output, and risks.
- [ ] No secrets, tokens, or PII in code, fixtures, logs, or the PR description.

## Evidence block (paste into the PR)

```
## Verification
- npx @protonspy/csdd spec test-report <feature> --run --lang <lang>   ✅  (tests + coverage evidence)
- <lint command>      ✅
- <typecheck command> ✅
- <build command>     ✅
```

If any box cannot be checked, the work is not done — report the blocked item
explicitly rather than claiming completion.
